<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nicolas Rolin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1376–<a href="/years/1462">1462</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nicolas Rolin was chancellor of the Burgundian state under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good</a> from 1422 until shortly before his death in 1462. A lawyer from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/autun">Autun</a>, he directed the government of lands stretching from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> to Holland and negotiated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-arras-1435">Treaty of Arras</a> of 1435. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hospices-de-beaune">Hospices de Beaune</a> in 1443 and is shown in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-van-eyck">Jan van Eyck</a>'s Madonna of Chancellor Rolin.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nicolas-rolin.jpg" alt="Nicolas Rolin" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan van Eyck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jan_van_Eyck_071.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
